A series of attacks carried out by Yemen's Houthis using ballistic missiles and drones wounded 13 civilians in southern Saudi Arabia on Tuesday. Meanwhile the US Defence Department's inspector general revealed that the United States is facing a shortfall in ammunition as a result of its costly war in Iran. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81d8b47c-b0b2-11f1-b0b2-c3058f5430ea</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 03:06:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42024f72-b07e-11f1-8db3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84H89F.jpg">© Mohammed Huwais, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy meetings in Texas at US's invitation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation</link><description>
A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a5aff92-b0af-11f1-8158-3570f775cb63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:44:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg">© Ronaldo Schemidt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7fd1a90-b0a2-11f1-b996-bf02f22ad66f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:51:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/def44e4c-b09d-11f1-be01-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg">© Saul Loeb, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Trump calls concerns over rogue AI a 'hoax' promoted by a ‘SICK conspiracy’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-trump-calls-concerns-over-rogue-ai-a-hoax-promoted-by-a-sick-conspiracy</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Monday rejected warnings about the risks of artificial intelligence, calling concerns over rogue AI part of a “SICK conspiracy” as tech leaders urge greater safeguards. The clash comes as the rapidly advancing technology faces scrutiny over cybersecurity, jobs, data centres and its potential impact on national security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b79f91a-b08a-11f1-ac1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T021020Z-1000114421-RC2MINA0CLDT-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b79f91a-b08a-11f1-ac1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T021020Z-1000114421-RC2MINA0CLDT-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9122e120-b0a1-11f1-b807-bf02f22ad66f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:05:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b79f91a-b08a-11f1-ac1f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-14T021020Z-1000114421-RC2MINA0CLDT-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-IRELAND.jpg">© Kylie Cooper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Dangote refinery launches Africa’s biggest IPO for retail investors</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-dangote-refinery-launches-africa-biggest-ipo-for-retail-investors</link><description>
Africa’s richest man Aliko Dangote on Monday launched an IPO for his $19 billion Nigerian oil refinery, seeking $1.6 billion from retail investors across the continent. The offering values Africa’s largest refinery at about $49 billion and has drawn both strong investor interest and concerns over its high valuation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17aad168-b05b-11f1-b58b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/732cb7dc19c595839564de7f85f58c87ed0476c1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17aad168-b05b-11f1-b58b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/732cb7dc19c595839564de7f85f58c87ed0476c1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b86e24c-b099-11f1-93af-6b224e4d46e2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:05:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17aad168-b05b-11f1-b58b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/732cb7dc19c595839564de7f85f58c87ed0476c1.jpg">© Toyin Adedokun, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes</link><description>
Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a838820a-b08f-11f1-b656-b3452f437d0f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:57:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/183b4120-b084-11f1-9cad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239577216137.jpg">© Aurel Obreja, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks</link><description>
American rapper Macklemore announced on Monday that he was dropped from Ed Sheeran’s US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83b4b46c-b08a-11f1-b5e0-b3452f437d0f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:20:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d38d806-b078-11f1-b9cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1729ad2e072996a142da7b053ef29307fba83d5a.jpg">© Arnaud Finistre, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time</link><description>
The US Space Force has confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22322948-b087-11f1-ad6a-db263a3e2d74</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:56:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54b1beee-a432-11f1-8b6d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-29T195602Z-94810877-RC2I8NAYVGKF-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-NASA-TELESCOPE.jpg">© Joe Skipper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bob Mackie, fashion designer for the stars, dies at 87</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bob-mackie-fashion-designer-for-the-stars-dies-at-87</link><description>
⁠Hollywood designer ⁠Bob Mackie, ​known for making stars such as Cher and ​Elton John sparkle, died on Monday at 87, according to a post on his official Instagram account. His career ​spanned ‌five decades and included ⁠designing a Barbie doll clothes collection. FRANCE 24's Camille Knight has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e195dc4-b084-11f1-8915-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-231210-231352-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e195dc4-b084-11f1-8915-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-231210-231352-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b7c982-b084-11f1-8e8d-db263a3e2d74</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:40:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Rights group accuses Israel of dismantling 'Palestinian existence' in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli rights group B'Tselem said Monday that Israeli actions in the occupied West Bank form part of a greater project designed to make it impossible for Palestinians to exist together as a people. In a report titled "The Elimination Project", the group alleged five connected Israeli tactics and policies in the West Bank: "violence, ethnic cleansing, movement restrictions, economic strangulation, social and political destruction". FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5d3dc4-b080-11f1-8b78-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-230418-230604-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5d3dc4-b080-11f1-8b78-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-230418-230604-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4964844-b080-11f1-bc80-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:26:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Yemen: Fact-checking videos claiming to show Houthi rebel attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1</link><description>
A video claiming to show Houthi rebels ambushing Saudi-backed mercenaries has racked up major views on X. But the FRANCE 24 Observers found it is actually footage of 2024 Houthi military drills. The clip was edited with football commentary and blurred flags, which originally show Israel, the UK and US, not Saudi Arabia. Other viral videos falsely linked to Houthi attacks on a Saudi Aramco refinery were also traced to unrelated fires in Texas and Russia. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799a26da-b07e-11f1-9b60-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6257860516aa85f0346da31-02858738.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799a26da-b07e-11f1-9b60-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6257860516aa85f0346da31-02858738.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f9ccada-b07e-11f1-a49c-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:10:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says</link><description>
Turkish police on Sunday swooped on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan lashing it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb447d6-b07e-11f1-b32d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-223110-224619-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb447d6-b07e-11f1-b32d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-223110-224619-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5ebc17a-b07f-11f1-82d6-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:02:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Monte FRANCIS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Nigeria's Dangote refinery kicks off blockbuster IPO</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260914-nigeria-s-dangote-refinery-kicks-off-blockbuster-ipo</link><description>
Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote launched the biggest-ever share sale on the African continent, listing 4.1 billion shares in his Lagos refinery on the stock exchange.  He framed it as a "people's IPO" to give all Nigerians a chance to share the plant's wealth potentials. Trading is expected to start in November. Meanwhile, global oil prices continued to advance as attacks by Yemen's Houthi rebels forced Saudi Arabia to shut down its East-West oil pipeline. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f137b4ca-b07c-11f1-9abb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11066529056aa85c710aa835-00283286.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f137b4ca-b07c-11f1-9abb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11066529056aa85c710aa835-00283286.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cda3672-b07c-11f1-a9f6-e5693c06a267</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:46:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Nigerian oil refinery Dangote aims to raise 1.6 billion dollars</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nigerian-oil-refinery-dangote-aims-to-raise-1-6-billion-dollars</link><description>
In tonight's edition, Nigeria's Dangote refinery opens itself to public ownership with plans to raise 1.6 billion dollars from retail investors across the continent. Also, President Felix Tshisekedi calls on the National Service to clean up the streets of Kinshasa. And with a month and a half to go until the Youth Olympic Games begin, the Olympic flame begins its tour of Senegal, the tournament's host country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62c362ea-b07a-11f1-be3d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DN196787-A-01-20260908-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62c362ea-b07a-11f1-be3d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DN196787-A-01-20260908-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fded387c-b07a-11f1-843e-69c181e861bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:31:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clémence WALLER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas</link><description>
Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a0dfe5c-b072-11f1-a476-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8AY39E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a0dfe5c-b072-11f1-a476-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8AY39E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87afc0c8-b073-11f1-a63d-8187002fc3b1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:54:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a0dfe5c-b072-11f1-a476-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8AY39E.jpg">© Murat Kocabas, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Axis of Iranian centrality' remains "one of more destabilising forces in the region", expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis launched a fresh barrage of missile and drone attacks on Saudi military targets on Monday, as Iran denied any involvement in the country's revived civil war. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr H. A. Hellyer, Senior Fellow in Geopolitics, International Security, and Middle East Studies at the Royal United Services Institute, says that Iran and its non-state proxies "remain to be one of the more destabilising forces in the region alongside the Israeli project of regional paramountcy".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/001ebad8-b073-11f1-a1cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-210414-211512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/001ebad8-b073-11f1-a1cc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-210414-211512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0590cab0-b073-11f1-8e4b-f178ef1761fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:46:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Leaders urge EU to boost Arctic role to tackle Russia 'threat'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat</link><description>
Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a70e00e8-077b-11f1-9159-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-21T100746Z-426063708-RC2Q9T9RM703-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GREENLAND-ARCTIC-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a70e00e8-077b-11f1-9159-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-21T100746Z-426063708-RC2Q9T9RM703-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GREENLAND-ARCTIC-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c26be16-b06d-11f1-84d9-f7a544c1e209</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:06:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Where is the kill switch? AI doomsday warnings trigger calls to regulate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260914-where-is-the-kill-switch-ai-doomsday-warnings-trigger-calls-to-regulate</link><description>
Talk about doomsday scrolling. In the past week, our timelines have been alight with dark predictions of our imminent demise, including the one by a Silicon Valley engineer who puts a number on the chances of artificial intelligence wiping out humanity. Better than 10-percent. Triggering the wave of panic, the recent breach of the machine-learning programmers' site Hugging Face by AI machines who banded together to keep their nefarious deeds secret from their human overlords. Can machines actually destroy the planet on their own? In the age of technology, does problem solving always override safety? 
